Supplements work best when they become routine. It isn't one day's dose that changes anything, but the habit of taking the right dose, at the right time, for long enough.

This material brings together three Paker Health supplements that cover different fronts: energy for training, skin and strength. For each one, what it does in the body, what research shows and how to fit it into your day.

## 1. Pre-workout gives your training more energy

A good pre-workout brings together ingredients that work on different fronts, and **caffeine** is the star. It helps increase alertness and improve concentration. The International Society of Sports Nutrition position stand by Guest and colleagues (2021) shows that caffeine improves performance both in people who have trained for years and in beginners.

The other ingredients round out the team. Arginine is a precursor of nitric oxide, which is linked to blood vessel dilation. Beta-alanine builds carnosine in muscle, which helps buffer the acidity of hard efforts, as the same society's position stand describes (Trexler and colleagues, 2015). Taurine, an amino acid common in energy drinks, improved endurance in a meta-analysis by Waldron and colleagues (2018). And tyrosine is the raw material for dopamine and noradrenaline, both linked to focus.

In FortPaker, all five come together in a 10 g serving. Take it 30 to 60 minutes before training, mixed in water.

> It contains caffeine: avoid it close to bedtime, during pregnancy and if you are sensitive to stimulants.

## 2. Collagen needs consistency to show on your skin

Collagen is the protein that gives skin its structure, and the body makes less of it as we age. Supplements bring hydrolyzed collagen, broken down into small **peptides** the gut can absorb.

In a study by Proksch and colleagues (2014), women aged 45 to 65 who took 2.5 g of collagen peptides a day for 8 weeks had smaller wrinkles around the eyes than the group that took a placebo. The detail that matters is time: skin renews itself slowly, and results show up in weeks, not days.

Vitamin C is there because it helps form collagen, and zinc helps maintain skin, hair and nails. Collagenpaker brings together 2.5 g of peptides, vitamin C, zinc, selenium and hyaluronic acid in a 5 g serving. The secret is making it a habit: the same time every day, mixed into water or juice.

## 3. Creatine isn't just for bodybuilders

Creatine is one of the most studied supplements in the world. Your body already makes creatine and stores it in muscle, where it becomes **phosphocreatine**, the energy reserve for short, intense efforts. That is why it helps increase physical performance in repeated short, high-intensity exercise, like sprints, jumps and strength sets.

The International Society of Sports Nutrition position stand by Kreider and colleagues (2017) concluded that creatine monohydrate brings benefits from teenagers to older adults and is safe for healthy people, with no serious side effects. At 3 to 5 g a day, muscle stores fill up in 3 to 4 weeks.

You don't need to take it before training: the effect comes from full stores, not from when you take the dose. CreaPaker is micronized creatine monohydrate, which mixes easily into water, juice or a shake.

:::list-icon
barbell | **Pre-workout 30 to 60 minutes before.** That is the time caffeine needs to kick in for your session.
sparkles | **Collagen every day for 8 weeks.** Skin shows results slowly.
flash | **Creatine, 3 to 5 g, at any time.** What counts is keeping your stores full.
:::

Pick a fixed time for each one and let the routine do the rest.

